/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - In the rectifying section above the feed, liquid L flows down and vapour V rises.
   - y is vapour mole fraction of the more volatile component; x is liquid mole fraction; R = L/D is the reflux ratio; xD is distillate mole fraction.
   - Below the feed, the stripping section has its own operating line.
   - L′ and V′ are stripping-section liquid and vapour molar flows; B is bottoms molar flow; xB is bottoms mole fraction.
   - q measures the thermal state of the feed.
   - xF is feed mole fraction; q is the feed thermal state defined above; the slope of the line is q/(q−1).
   - The q-line is not an operating line.
   - Use a y-x diagram.
   - y* is vapour mole fraction in equilibrium with liquid x; α is relative volatility; x is liquid mole fraction.
   - Draw the diagonal y = x.
*/
