/* book exam traps: Stepping horizontally to the operating line instead of the equilibrium curve. The horizontal move gives the equilibrium liquid x* at the current vapour y; the vertical move gives the next operating-line y. | Counting the partial reboiler twice, or not counting it at all. The last step that crosses xB includes one equilibrium stage for the reboiler. | Treating the q-line as an operating line. It only locates the feed intersection P; the operating lines are the rectifying and stripping lines. | Switching operating lines at xF when the feed is not saturated liquid. Switch where the step passes xP, the x of the operating-line intersection; xP = xF only when q = 1. */
