/* book: lead: Reflux is the liquid returned from the condenser to the top of the column, and the reflux ratio R = L/D compares it with the distillate D. R sets the main trade-off of distillation: more reflux needs fewer stages but more reboiler steam and condenser water. At minimum reflux the stage count is infinite; at total reflux it is the smallest possible but no product leaves. Designers work between the t */
/* book Figure 4.5.1: Left: the stage count for the worked example, stepped off at each reflux ratio. It falls from infinity at Rmin = 1.444 toward Nmin = 6.43 and is 14 whole stages at 1.3 Rmin. Right: a simple annual cost, one unit per stage plus six units per unit of (R + 1); its flat minimum lies between 1.2 and 1.5  */
