/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Vapour from the top tray is condensed.
   - R is the reflux ratio; L is the reflux flow (kmol/h); D is the distillate flow (kmol/h); V is the vapour flow to the condenser (kmol/h).
   - On the y-x diagram the rectifying operating line has slope R/(R + 1) and intercept xD/(R + 1) (see McCabe-Thiele).
   - Lowering R moves the operating line toward the equilibrium curve.
   - For an ideal-shaped curve the pinch sits where the q-line meets the equilibrium curve, at (x′, y′).
   - x′, y′ are the pinch coordinates on the equilibrium curve (mole fractions); xD is the distillate mole fraction.
   - For a saturated-vapour feed the q-line is horizontal at y = xF, so y′ = xF and x′ is the liquid in equilibrium with it.
   - At total reflux no distillate is drawn and all condensate returns, so R → ∞ and both operating lines lie on the diagonal y = x.
   - Nmin is the minimum number of theoretical stages, including the reboiler; xD, xB are distillate and bottoms mole fractions of the more volatile component; α is the relative volatility.
   - Real columns need product, so R is finite.
*/
