/* book exam traps: Using Rmin as the working reflux: the stage count is infinite there. | Reporting the Fenske Nmin as the stage count at Ropt; Fenske holds only at total reflux (6.4 against 14 in the example). | Applying Rmin = (xD − yF*)/(yF* − xF) to a vapour or two-phase feed; it is for q = 1 only. Use the q-line pinch (x′, y′) otherwise. | Missing a tangent pinch on a non-ideal curve: check that the minimum-reflux line does not cut the equilibrium curve anywhere above the feed. | Rounding Rmin to 1.44 and then multiplying: 1.3 × 1.444 = 1.878, not 1.872. Carry three decimals until the end. */
