/* book exam traps: Putting ΔD on a saturated curve. It is fixed by xD and the condenser balance and lies above the H curve. | Using H and h per mole of one component. They are per mole of mixture; a mole of mixture changes composition. | Reading HΔD as the condenser duty. HΔD = hD + QC/D, so the duty per mole of distillate is HΔD − hD (72.9 kJ/mol in the worked example). | Placing ΔB above the h curve. It normally lies below because the reboiler adds heat. | Locating ΔB independently of ΔD. For a given feed, ΔD, F and ΔB are collinear; ΔB is where that line meets x = xB. */
